  "spec": "Security review T-1607 approved T-1606 but found guidance trimmed beyond the spec (only the orchestrate skill had a token budget). Restore it, tersely; touch nothing else.\n\n1. CLAUDE.md step 5 (line 18): the parenthesis becomes '(keep ## Now current: goal, next step, open human decisions; under 10k chars; auto-handover section last; status lines go to .orchestrator/plan-log.md, which resumes do not read)'.\n2. CLAUDE.md step 9 (line 22): 'the session compacts in place' becomes 'the session compacts in place (launcher --autocompact, or /compact from Remote Control or the terminal while the session is idle)'.\n3. .orchestrator/prompts/planner.md mirrors the CLAUDE.md lists; apply the same two edits there.\n4. skills/planner/resume/SKILL.md line 20: 'status lines are in .orchestrator/plan-log.md' becomes 'status lines are in .orchestrator/plan-log.md; do not read it, grep it only for a missing fact'. tests/test_skills_compaction.py checks L2 tokens per skill against a baseline: if resume goes over, shorten other wording in that file without losing a rule; never raise the baseline.\nRun tests/test_goals.py, tests/test_hooks.py, tests/test_skills_compaction.py and tests/test_skill_eval.py and commit.",
